Apple today announced that its <a href="https://www.apple.com/uk/retail/festivalplace/">Festival Place store</a> in Basingstoke, England will be permanently closing on Saturday, November 21.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-Festival-Place-scaled.jpeg" alt="" width="2560" height="1433" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075367" /><em>Apple Festival Place</em></div><br/>
Apple had <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/13/apple-closing-basingstoke-store/">already announced that the store would be closing</a> in November, but it had not provided the public with a specific date until now.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's store inside the Festival Place shopping center opened in 2011, so it had a 15-year run.<br/>
<br/>
In a statement <a href="https://www.readingchronicle.co.uk/news/26461351.fully-redesigned-apple-store-set-reopen-reading/">shared with <em>The Reading Chronicle</em></a> in August, Apple said all employees at the Festival Place store would have the opportunity to work at <a href="https://www.apple.com/uk/retail/theoracle/">Apple The Oracle</a> in nearby Reading, England or at other Apple Store locations in the country.<br/>
<br/>
